{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5423) to implement `cmd/touch` covering SRD062 requirements R1.1 through R1.4 (the \"Default behavior and file creation\" group only). This is part of the go-unix-utils project, which reimplements GNU coreutils in Go with differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The specific requirements are:\n   - R1.1: Update access and modification times of each file to the current time\n   - R1.2: Create empty files with default permissions when they don't exist\n   - R1.3: `-c` or `--no-create` suppresses file creation; no error if file doesn't exist\n   - R1.4: Support multiple file arguments, processing each in order\n\n   Two files must be created: `cmd/touch/main.go` and `cmd/touch/touch_test.go`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils verified via differential testing\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` compares Go binary output against GNU reference binary (gtouch)\n   - `pkg/testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` compiles cmd/ package for testing\n   - `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` must be called at start of main\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gtouch\")` with `t.Skip` if reference binary not found\n   - LC_ALL=C environment for deterministic test output\n   - Copyright header required: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max\n   - File size limit: 500 lines max\n   - No git commands allowed (orchestrator manages git)\n   - Write all files before running build/test commands\n   - Non-goals from SRD: no `--time=WORD` standalone flag, no obsolescent `-t` format with two-digit years\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/soft