{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01552fpkMbBheBA4WbQwsc1H","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now let me create a comprehensive summary of the patterns I found:\n\n## Summary: cmd/cat as a Pattern Example\n\nI found an excellent pattern example in **cmd/cat**. Here are the key details:\n\n### 1. Flag Parsing (Custom Implementation)\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5423/cmd/cat/main.go` (lines 55-104)\n\nThe project uses **custom flag parsing** (not Go's flag package or pflag):\n- `parseFlags()` function manually parses command-line arguments\n- Maintains individual boolean variables (`flagN`, `flagB`, `flagS`, `flagV`, `flagE`, `flagT`)\n- Handles combined flags (e.g., `-Aet` expands to multiple flags)\n- Supports `--` to end flag processing\n- Special handling for dash (`-`) to represent stdin\n- Unknown flags print to stderr and exit(1)\n\n### 2. Main Function Structure\n```go\nfunc main() {\n    sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()  // Signal handling\n    \n    args := parseFlags(os.Args[1:])\n    if len(args) == 0 {\n        args = []string{\"-\"}  // Default to stdin\n    }\n    \n    exitCode := 0\n    for _, name := range args {\n        // Process each file\n        if err != nil {\n            // Handle errors\n            exitCode = 1\n        }\n    }\n    if exitCode != 0 {\n        os.Exit(exitCode)\n    }\n}\n```\n\nKey patterns:\n- Early return 0 if successful (implicit, no explicit exit call)\n- Only exit with non-zero on errors\n- Uses `syscall.EPIPE` error check to exit cleanly when pipe closes\n- Installs signal handlers for proper cleanup\n\n### 3. Test Patterns\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5423/cmd/cat/cat_test.go`\n\nUses the `testutils` package:\n- `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` - Builds the current package binary for testing\n- `testutils.DiffTest{}` - Test struct with: `Name`, `Args`, `Stdin`, `WorkDir`\n- `testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)` - Compares implementation against reference binary (gcat)\n- Custom assertions for error cases (exit codes, stderr output)\n- Fixture files created with `t.TempDir()` and `os.WriteFile()`\n\n### 4. Copyright Header Format\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n// cmd/<name> implements <spec>: <description>.\npackage main\n```\n\nStandard format across all utilities in the cmd/ directory.\n\n### Key File Paths\n- **Main implementation:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5423/cmd/cat/main.go`\n- **Tests:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5423/cmd/cat/cat_test.go`\n- **Test utilities:** Package `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils`"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c63cf3bc-8fc1-4dca-8141-cf5e08409ea1","uuid":"e579adb3-e317-42af-9b46-0a23afa43658","timestamp":"2026-05-21T14:38:08.242Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5423, find an existing cmd/ utility that's a good example of flag parsing and file operations. Look at a simple one like cmd/mkdir or cmd/rm or cmd/cat — read its main.go and test file to understand the patterns used. I need to see:\n1. How flags are parsed (flag package vs pflag vs custom)\n2. How the main function is structured\n3. How tests use DiffTest and BuildBinary\n4. The copyright header format\n\nSearch breadth: quick","agentId":"a2c5c0b194cf68651","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now let me create a comprehensive summary of the patterns I found:\n\n## Summary: cmd/cat as a Pattern Example\n\nI found an excellent pattern example in **cmd/cat**. Here are the key details:\n\n### 1. Flag Parsing (Custom Implementation)\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5423/cmd/cat/main.go` (lines 55-104)\n\nThe project uses **custom flag parsing** (not Go's flag package or pflag):\n- `parseFlags()` function manually parses command-line arguments\n- Maintains individual boolean variables (`flagN`, `flagB`, `flagS`, `flagV`, `flagE`, `flagT`)\n- Handles combined flags (e.g., `-Aet` expands to multiple flags)\n- Supports `--` to end flag processing\n- Special handling for dash (`-`) to represent stdin\n- Unknown flags print to stderr and exit(1)\n\n### 2. Main Function Structure\n```go\nfunc main() {\n    sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()  // Signal handling\n    \n    args := parseFlags(os.Args[1:])\n    if len(args) == 0 {\n        args = []string{\"-\"}  // Default to stdin\n    }\n    \n    exitCode := 0\n    for _, name := range args {\n        // Process each file\n        if err != nil {\n            // Handle errors\n            exitCode = 1\n        }\n    }\n    if exitCode != 0 {\n        os.Exit(exitCode)\n    }\n}\n```\n\nKey patterns:\n- Early return 0 if successful (implicit, no explicit exit call)\n- Only exit with non-zero on errors\n- Uses `syscall.EPIPE` error check to exit cleanly when pipe closes\n- Installs signal handlers for proper cleanup\n\n### 3. Test Patterns\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5423/cmd/cat/cat_test.go`\n\nUses the `testutils` package:\n- `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` - Builds the current package binary for testing\n- `testutils.DiffTest{}` - Test struct with: `Name`, `Args`, `Stdin`, `WorkDir`\n- `testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)` - Compares implementation against reference binary (gcat)\n- Custom assertions for error cases (exit codes, stderr output)\n- Fixture files created with `t.TempDir()` and `os.WriteFile()`\n\n### 4. Copyright Header Format\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserve